-- title:
--   Positions moving backward by one unit
-- statement:
--   For a permutation $p$ of $n$ linearly ordered positions, define the backward unit set by the condition $p(i)+1=i$, interpreted in natural representatives. Thus the position moves exactly one step left in the finite interval. Position zero cannot belong, and this condition does not include cyclic wrapping. The definition is meaningful also for the empty set of positions. It isolates the unit backward moves used in finite drop budgets.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/snow-ghost/glushkov-lx-lean/blob/8cddcd222b591673dc63475d9d45b9ed5c6eb92c/LX/FiniteDropBudget.lean#L10-L11

